\## 8. Automatic Application Processing\
\
When a student submits an application:\
\
1\. Validate the submitted information.\
2\. Save the application in the database.\
3\. Generate a unique application ID.\
4\. Automatically assign a registration number.\
5\. Generate a roll number according to the admission session and class.\
6\. Generate a professional one-page A4 application PDF.\
7\. Allow the applicant to download the PDF.\
8\. Show application status.\
9\. Allow the applicant to track the application.\
\
Registration number format:\
\
\*\*GZMS0001\*\*\
\
Rules:\
\- First four characters: GZMS.\
\- Last four characters: sequential number.\
\- First registration number: GZMS0001.\
\- Next: GZMS0002, GZMS0003, and so on.\
\- Never duplicate registration numbers.\
\- Generate numbers securely on the server/database.\
\
Roll number:\
\- Begin from 0001.\
\- Maintain a unique roll within the relevant academic session and class.\
\- Never assign duplicate active rolls within the same class/session.\
\
Do not confuse the application ID, registration number and class roll number.\
\
